  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 309.01 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 309.01 Applicability. The rules in this part shall apply as follows:\n\n(a) Env-Or 309.02 shall apply to any AST system designed and used to store oil in the solid phase at atmospheric temperature and pressure;\n\n(b) Env-Or 309.03 shall apply to any location where any oil-filled electrical equipment individually contains more than 660 gallons of oil;\n\n(c) Env-Or 309.04 shall apply to any AST system with an oil storage capacity of more than 660 gallons but not more than 1,320 gallons that:\n\n(1) Is included in Env-Or 301.02(a)(1) but not in Env-Or 301.02(a)(2);\n\n(2) Is located at a construction site; and\n\n(3) Is installed and exists only for the specific duration of the construction contract for which it is used, not to exceed one year;\n\n(d) Env-Or 309.05 shall apply to any AST having a capacity of not more than 330 gallons that:\n\n(1) Contains heating oil for on-premise heating only; and\n\n(2) Is at an AST facility that is included in Env-Or 301.02(a); and\n\n(e) Env-Or 309.06 shall apply to use of cargo trucks by industrial enterprises or the military.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
}
